# Mythos Project Guidance

Mythos is a Factorio 2.0 Lua mod for pocket dimensions. Before changing runtime
code, read `ARCHITECTURE.md`; it is the maintainer map for entry points,
packages, compatibility wrappers, persisted names, and manual smoke tests.

## Runtime Map

- `control.lua` should stay thin: lifecycle hooks plus event registration.
- Runtime packages live under `script/bootstrap`, `script/events`,
  `script/mythos`, `script/pocket_dimension`, `script/clone`,
  `script/virtual_chest`, `script/power`, `script/migrations`, and `script/ui`.
- Top-level files such as `script/Mythos.lua`, `script/PocketDimension.lua`,
  `script/virtualChest.lua`, `script/maintenance.lua`, `script/electricity.lua`,
  and old UI/module names are compatibility wrappers. New implementation code
  should require the package paths directly.

## Save Compatibility

Do not rename storage keys, surface names, prototype names, setting names, custom
input names, or blueprint tag names without adding a migration. Important keys
include `storage.mythoi`, `storage.saved_dimensions`, `storage.virtualChests`,
`storage.mythos_next_snapshot_id`, and `storage.mythos_pending_paste`.

Preserve legacy migration paths for `mythos-inventory`, `lab-dark-2`,
`storage.mythos_storage_anchors`, `storage.mythos_inventories`, and
`storage.virtual_chests`.

## Refactor Rules

- Prefer focused modules and facades over re-growing monolithic files.
- Keep compatibility wrappers until there is a deliberate cleanup/migration.
- Avoid `goto` patterns; use structured conditionals to stay Lua-load safe.
- Keep Factorio API behavior stable unless the user explicitly asks for gameplay
  changes.
- When changing clone, blueprint, power, migrations, or virtual chest code, treat
  it as high-risk and review storage and save/load behavior carefully.

## Verification

There is no automated test suite in this repo. At minimum run static checks such
as `git diff --check`, stale require searches, and IDE diagnostics. If Lua tools
or Factorio are available, also run syntax/load checks. Use the smoke-test matrix
in `ARCHITECTURE.md` before considering gameplay-sensitive changes release-ready.
